UID:74b876a7ef2e144f@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair an
 d Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP f
 or Commandants: Soldiers: Commandant — Costume (you provide): Black Se
 amless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Mak
 eup: Men's Light Stage Makeup Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out 
 of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Whit
 e Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): White gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction
  Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shado
 w applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Bla
 ck eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the che
 eks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the 
 stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n
 •  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n• 
  Brown or tan under cheek bone to create shadow and accentuate the jaw l
 ine\n•  Brown eye liner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipstick
 \n• *Men will not look like they are wearing makeup. It will help the 
 face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tight
 s and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle
  costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate f
 abrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume 
 damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Ne
 ver throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by the
 ir elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in co
 stume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any c
 ostume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume 
 and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume du
 ring its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or colog
 ne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast
  member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in cost
 ume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from t
 heir assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bob
 by pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• 
  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with
  any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do
  not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage 
 or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
